  ],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If an effect gives the enchanted creature flying after Tightening Coils became attached to it, the creature will have flying.","oracle_id":"71af7e54-e22d-4354-a35c-80e4e5f4031c","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Colossus Hammer can be attached to a creature that didn't have flying to begin with. It just won't lose flying.","oracle_id":"8ec03b88-8d3a-4a32-8b7c-7da59b0c03d0","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an ability of the equipped creature states that it has flying \"as long as\" a particular condition is true, that condition becoming true will not cause that creature to gain flying. For example, if the equipped creature \"has flying as long as it's attacking,\" it will not gain flying, even if it attacks after Colossus Hammer becomes attached to it.","oracle_id":"8ec03b88-8d3a-4a32-8b7c-7da59b0c03d0","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the equipped creature gains flying after Colossus Hammer became attached to it, it will keep flying.","oracle_id":"8ec03b88-8d3a-4a32-8b7c-7da59b0c03d0","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To work as an evasion ability, an attacking creature must already have flying when the declare blockers step begins. Once a creature has become blocked, giving it flying won’t change that.","oracle_id":"f7518456-45ed-41d4-bd3c-5aacea28eb35","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Combat damage is the damage that’s dealt automatically by attacking and blocking creatures, even if it’s redirected (by Harm’s Way, perhaps). Noncombat damage is any other damage (generally, it’s damage dealt as the result of a spell or ability).","oracle_id":"fc24af7b-f3d0-41d0-aaac-d83424455717","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Magebane Armor can equip a creature that doesn’t have flying. The “lose flying” effect just won’t do anything in that case.","oracle_id":"fc24af7b-f3d0-41d0-aaac-d83424455717","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Magebane Armor causes the equipped creature to lose flying at the time it became equipped. Any ability that grants that creature flying that starts to work later (such as a Jump that resolves later, or a Levitation that comes under your control later) will work normally.","oracle_id":"fc24af7b-f3d0-41d0-aaac-d83424455717","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
